# Plan: Fix Telegram Bot Timing Issue

The bot currently sends scheduled messages based on the server's local time (UTC), which causes them to arrive 5 hours early for the user (UTC-5). This plan introduces robust timezone handling using the `pytz` library.

## Proposed Changes

### [telegram-study-bot]

#### [MODIFY] [requirements.txt](file:///C:/Users/Antonio/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/Mis%20Proyectos%20Antigravity/telegram-study-bot/requirements.txt)
- Add `pytz` to the dependencies.

#### [MODIFY] [bot.py](file:///C:/Users/Antonio/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/Mis%20Proyectos%20Antigravity/telegram-study-bot/bot.py)
- Import `pytz`.
- Use `os.getenv("TIMEZONE", "America/Bogota")` to determine the target timezone.
- Update [motor_tiempo](file:///C:/Users/Antonio/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/Mis%20Proyectos%20Antigravity/telegram-study-bot/bot.py#334-347) to use `datetime.now(pytz.timezone(target_tz))` instead of `datetime.now()`.
- Update [guardar_archivo_id](file:///C:/Users/Antonio/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/Mis%20Proyectos%20Antigravity/telegram-study-bot/bot.py#64-83) and [_actualizar_cache_sefaria](file:///C:/Users/Antonio/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/Mis%20Proyectos%20Antigravity/telegram-study-bot/bot.py#160-204) to also use the correct timezone for consistency.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Create `verify_timezone.py` to:
    1. Print the current UTC time.
    2. Print the current time in the configured timezone (e.g., `America/Bogota`).
    3. Verify that the offset matches expectations (5 hours difference).
- Run the script: `python verify_timezone.py`

### Manual Verification
- The user should set the `TIMEZONE` environment variable in Railway to their preferred timezone (e.g., `America/Bogota`).
- The user can verify the next scheduled message arrives at the correct local time.
